      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_c109fabf",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: i_refuse_to_debate_gun_control_meme; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The meme depicts a man in cowboy attire holding a rope, with text stating 'i refuse to debate gun control with folks who eat soap and are confused on which pisser to use.' The text uses degrading, offensive language to describe opponents of gun control, implying they are mentally incompetent or irrational. This is a hateful meme as it targets a specific group (those opposing gun control) with derogatory and demeaning language, aiming to delegitimize their views through insult rather than reasoned argument. The visual of the cowboy may be used to imply a certain stereotype (e.g., rural, traditional, or gun-owning), but the core toxicity lies in the verbal attack on the opposing viewpoint, which is a form of hate speech directed at a political or ideological group.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_a7b8a3d6"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
